{"id":"h10t4","name":"Prorated Subscription Invoices","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["plans","events"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p><code>plans</code> gives the monthly price of each plan in cents. <code>events</code> is a list of strings <code>\"YYYY-MM-DD customer ACTION\"</code> or <code>\"YYYY-MM-DD customer ACTION plan\"</code>, sorted by date (several events can share a date; apply them in the order of the list):</p>\n<ul><li><code>START plan</code>: the customer becomes active on this plan from this day included. If the customer is already active, it is the same as <code>CHANGE</code>.</li>\n<li><code>CHANGE plan</code>: from this day included, the customer is on the new plan. Ignored if the customer is not active.</li>\n<li><code>STOP</code>: the customer is not active any more from this day included (the last paid day is the day before). Ignored if the customer is not active.</li></ul>\n<p>A day is paid with the plan the customer has <b>at the end</b> of that day (after all the events of the day). The price of one day of a plan in a month is the monthly price divided by the number of days of that month (28 to 31). Customers who are still active are billed until the last day of the month of the <b>latest date</b> in <code>events</code>.</p>\n<p>The invoice of a customer for a month is the sum of its paid days, rounded to the nearest cent at the end (a half cent is rounded up). Your task is to return one string <code>\"customer,YYYY-MM,cents\"</code> per customer and month with at least one paid day, sorted by customer, then month.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>plans = {\"basic\": 3000, \"pro\": 9000, \"team\": 15500}</code></p><p><code>events = [\"2026-01-10 acme START basic\", \"2026-01-20 acme CHANGE pro\", \"2026-02-01 bolt START team\", \"2026-02-14 acme STOP\", \"2026-02-14 bolt CHANGE basic\", \"2026-02-14 bolt CHANGE team\", \"2026-03-03 bolt STOP\"]</code></p><p>the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"acme,2026-01,4452\", \"acme,2026-02,4179\", \"bolt,2026-02,15500\", \"bolt,2026-03,1000\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> dictionary plans<br><b>[input]</b> array.string events<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(plans, events):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["calendrier (jours par mois)","prorata au jour près","plusieurs événements le même jour","arrondi entier","datetime"],"minutes":35,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solution(plans, events)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Ici, la valeur attendue est une liste : compare ce que tu renvoies à « Expected return value » dans les résultats.</li><li>La comparaison est exacte (même type, mêmes valeurs, même ordre dans une liste), sauf les nombres décimaux, comparés à 0,000001 près.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 9 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"plans":{"basic":3000,"pro":9000,"team":15500},"events":["2026-01-10 acme START basic","2026-01-20 acme CHANGE pro","2026-02-01 bolt START team","2026-02-14 acme STOP","2026-02-14 bolt CHANGE basic","2026-02-14 bolt CHANGE team","2026-03-03 bolt STOP"]},"expected":{"value":["acme,2026-01,4452","acme,2026-02,4179","bolt,2026-02,15500","bolt,2026-03,1000"]}},{"input":{"plans":{"basic":3000,"pro":9000,"team":15500},"events":["2026-02-28 x START pro","2026-02-28 y CHANGE pro","2026-03-01 x START basic","2026-03-01 x STOP","2026-03-01 x START pro","2026-03-31 z STOP"]},"expected":{"value":["x,2026-02,321","x,2026-03,9000"]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}